String length() method in Java returns the length of the string. In this article, we will see how to find the length of a string using the String length() method.Example:
            Java

    class Geeks {
    public static void main(String[] args){

        String s1 = "abcd";
        System.out.println(s1.length());

        String s2 = "";
        System.out.println(s2.length());

        String s3 = "a";
        System.out.println(s3.length());
    }
}

